  "prefLabel": "He-P 4035.06 Notifications",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-18",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 4035.06 Notifications. A licensee shall notify the DHHS/RHS in writing within 30 days when an authorized user, an authorized nuclear pharmacist, a radiation safety officer, an associate radiation safety officer, an authorized medical physicist, or ophthalmic physicist permanently discontinues performance of duties under the license, or has a name change, has appointed a temporary radiation safety officer as provided in He-P 4035.10(d), or has appointed an associate radiation safety officer as provided in He-P 4035.10(c).\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for He-P 4035) #6942, eff 2-1-99; ss by #8800, INTERIM, eff 2-1-07, EXPIRED: 7-31-07\n\nNew. #8959, eff 8-7-07; ss by #10897, INTERIM, eff 7-22-15, EXPIRES: 1-18-16; ss by #11011, eff 1-15-16; ss by #13048, eff 6-2-20; ss by #13473, eff 10-25-22",
